---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import { ABOUT_DESCRIPTION, SITE_TITLE, YOUTUBE_CHANNEL } from '../consts';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead
			title={`About ${SITE_TITLE} | Stories & Creative Approach`}
			description={ABOUT_DESCRIPTION}
		/>
	</head>
	<body class="about-page">
		<a class="skip-link" href="#main-content">Skip to content</a>
		<SiteHeader />
		<main id="main-content" tabindex="-1">
			<header class="about-page__intro" data-reveal>
				<p class="eyebrow">About Petalwake</p>
				<h1>Stories matter<br /><em>because people do.</em></h1>
				<p class="about-page__lead">
					Petalwake Studios is a multidisciplinary creative studio shaped by storytelling,
					imagination, visual art, and a love of meaningful creative experiences.
				</p>
				<p>
					Our work can take many forms, from film, animation, and manga to music and illustrated stories.
					Christian faith is one of the roots of our perspective; here, we share those convictions
					alongside the creative approach that guides the studio.
				</p>
			</header>

			<section class="about-page__section about-page__section--light" aria-labelledby="foundation-title" data-reveal>
				<p class="eyebrow">What we believe</p>
				<div>
					<h2 id="foundation-title">The Creator is the source of every good thing.</h2>
					<p>
						God is the holy Creator and the source of all beauty, truth, and goodness. The heavens
						declare His glory (Psalm 19:1), and the beauty of creation can turn our attention toward
						the One who made it. Creativity is a gift: we seek to exercise it with care, to honor
						God and serve others.
					</p>
					<p>
						Every human being is made in God's image and possesses inherent dignity (Genesis
						1:26-27). People are worthy of compassion and also responsible for their choices.
						Human life holds the goodness of creation alongside the reality of sin, suffering,
						and brokenness; honest storytelling must make room for both.
					</p>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section class="about-page__section" aria-labelledby="grace-title" data-reveal>
				<p class="eyebrow">Grace and hope</p>
				<div>
					<h2 id="grace-title">The gospel gives shape to our hope.</h2>
					<p>
						Sin fractures our relationship with God and with one another. We believe forgiveness,
						redemption, and lasting hope are found in Jesus Christ, who gave Himself for sinners
						and rose from the dead. God's grace is not a reward for moral achievement; it is His
						gift, received through repentance and faith in Christ (Ephesians 2:8-9).
					</p>
					<p>
						This conviction informs the way we approach grief, love, injustice, responsibility,
						and forgiveness. Stories can explore these realities in distinct ways while reflecting
						the Christian perspective that informs the studio.
					</p>
					<p>
						Some projects may present the gospel directly; others may explore human experiences
						such as grief, responsibility, love, injustice, or forgiveness within the worldview
						that shapes the studio's perspective.
					</p>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section class="about-page__section about-page__section--inspiration" aria-labelledby="approach-title" data-reveal>
				<p class="eyebrow">Our creative approach</p>
				<div>
					<h2 id="approach-title">Image, sound, and meaning.</h2>
					<p>
						A landscape, a musical phrase, a lingering glance, or the silence between two people
						can carry meaning beyond dialogue. We bring image, sound, and atmosphere together in
						service of each story and the people within it.
					</p>
					<p>
						We are drawn to stories of imperfect people facing choices and consequences, and to
						the complexity of lives beyond a first impression. We want our work to attend to
						suffering without losing sight of beauty, and to portray hope without denying what hurts.
					</p>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section class="about-page__section about-page__section--light" aria-labelledby="scripture-title" data-reveal>
				<p class="eyebrow">A word from Scripture</p>
				<div>
					<h2 id="scripture-title">The heavens declare His glory.</h2>
					<blockquote>
						<p>“The heavens declare the glory of God; and the firmament sheweth his handywork.”</p>
						<cite>Psalm 19:1 (King James Version)</cite>
					</blockquote>
					<p>
						Psalm 19:1 gives voice to our conviction that creation speaks of God's glory. We
						approach each project as a chance to use creative gifts thoughtfully and serve our
						audience with honest, carefully made work.
					</p>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section class="about-page__section about-page__section--closing" aria-labelledby="looking-forward-title" data-reveal>
				<p class="eyebrow">The work ahead</p>
				<div>
					<h2 id="looking-forward-title">One story at a time.</h2>
					<p>
						Petalwake Studios is at the beginning. We are building a home for original stories
						and creative work, sharing what is ready today while making room for what comes next.
					</p>
					<p><a href="/work/">Explore the films <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></p>
					<p><a href="/gospel/">Read the gospel <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></p>
					<p><a href={YOUTUBE_CHANNEL} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Visit YouTube <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></p>
				</div>
			</section>
		</main>
		<SiteFooter />
	</body>
</html>
